What is Peat-free Compost?
Peat-free compost represents a sustainable alternative to traditional peat-based growing media, utilizing renewable materials like coconut coir, wood fiber, bark, green compost, and agricultural byproducts. These substitutes help preserve fragile peatland ecosystems, which store vast amounts of carbon. Widely adopted in gardening, organic farming, and commercial horticulture, peat-free compost meets rigorous sustainability certifications like RHS standards while maintaining essential plant-growing properties.
